.TH KERNELCUSTOM-MANAGER 1 "2026-11-01" "kernelcustom-manager 3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kernelcustom-manager \- build, sign and install custom Linux kernels
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kernelcustom-manager
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kernelcustom-manager
is a GTK4/libadwaita application for Debian that downloads Linux kernel
sources from kernel.org, configures and compiles them into Debian packages,
installs and removes kernels, manages
.I /usr/src
sources and GPU drivers, and signs kernels and modules for SecureBoot
with a Machine Owner Key (MOK).
.PP
Privileged operations go through
.I /usr/libexec/kernelcustom\-manager/kernelcustom\-helper
and are authorized by PolicyKit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/kernelcustom\-manager/
Working directory: sources, build logs, packages, profiles, MOK keys.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kernelcustom\-manager/language.conf
Interface language.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KCM_DATA_DIR
Use another working directory (for testing).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR mokutil (1)
